{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% from "_macros.html.j2" import ref with context %}
{% set h = q1.home %}
{% set fall = q2.CZE.fall %}
{% set yl = iv.q4.leagues %}
{% block title %}Czech Hockey Atlas{% endblock %}
{% block description %}An exploratory atlas of Czech professional hockey players per head against nine peer nations, 1995/96–{{ q1.season }}: counts per million, timing of changes, age and position, young players' share at home, players abroad, national-team rosters and goalkeepers. Public data, reproducible.{% endblock %}
{% block canonical %}https://hockey.bsandova.com/{% endblock %}
{% block head_extra %}
<script>
  /* The report used to be one page. Its old anchors (#q1 … #q7, #methodology, #autumn …) now live
     on their own pages: send an old link to the page that holds that part. */
  (function () {
    var map = {{ old_anchors|tojson }};
    var id = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));
    var to = map[id] || (id.indexOf('autumn-src-') === 0 ? 'this-autumn/#' + id : null);
    if (to) location.replace(to);
  })();
</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<a class="skip-link" href="#take">Skip to content</a>

<header class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="masthead-kicker">Research · Czech hockey atlas · 1995/96–{{ q1.season }}</p>
    <h1>Czech professional hockey players per head against nine peer nations, 1995/96–{{ q1.season }}</h1>
    <p class="masthead-deck">This exploratory atlas counts how many Czech players reach the NHL and Europe's four strongest leagues relative to population; in {{ q1.season }} Czechia ranked {{ ordinal(h.rank_nhl) }} of {{ q1.n_nations }} nations in the NHL.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="hero" id="summary">
  <img class="hero-photo" src="img/hockey.jpg" srcset="img/hockey-1200.jpg 1200w, img/hockey.jpg 1920w" sizes="100vw" alt="A hockey player carrying the puck across the ice, in black and white with only the blue of his jersey kept" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  <div class="container">
    <dl class="facts">
      <div class="fact"><dt>Czech NHL players per million, {{ q1.season }}</dt><dd><span class="fact-n">{{ f2(h.nhl_per_million) }}</span><span class="fact-note">{{ h.nhl }} players, population {{ f1(population_m) }} million · administrative count</span></dd></div>
      <div class="fact"><dt>NHL and rung-2 players per million</dt><dd><span class="fact-n">{{ f2(h.top5_per_million) }}</span><span class="fact-note">{{ h.top5 }} players · {{ ordinal(h.rank_top5) }} of {{ q1.n_nations }} · administrative count</span></dd></div>
      {% if fall %}<div class="fact"><dt>Downward step in the Czech NHL level</dt><dd><span class="fact-n">{{ times(fall.delta_factor.median) }}</span><span class="fact-note">90 % HDI {{ f2(fall.delta_factor.lo) }}–{{ f2(fall.delta_factor.hi) }} · most likely {{ fall.modal.season }} (p = {{ f2(fall.modal.prob) }})</span></dd></div>{% endif %}
      <div class="fact"><dt>Extraliga skater games played by skaters aged 20 or under</dt><dd><span class="fact-n">{{ pct(yl.Extraliga.games.mean) }}</span><span class="fact-note">95 % bootstrap by season {{ pct(yl.Extraliga.games.lo) }}–{{ pct(yl.Extraliga.games.hi) }} · {{ yl.Extraliga.games.seasons }} seasons</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <p class="hero-credit">Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jake_Levin_(Air_Force_Falcon%27s_men%27s_ice_hockey)_during_game_against_Bentley_Falcons_men%27s_ice_hockey_at_Cadet_Arena_in_Colorado_Springs_on_November_9,_2018_(45170233234).jpg">U.S. Air Force Academy</a> · public domain, colour held</p>
</section>

<section class="front-intro">
  <div class="container">
    <details class="tldr" open>
      <summary>Overwhelmed? Here's the short version</summary>
      <ul>
        <li>{{ q1.leaders_nhl[0].name }} and {{ q1.leaders_nhl[1].name }} have about {{ (([q1.leaders_nhl[0].nhl_per_million, q1.leaders_nhl[1].nhl_per_million]|min) / h.nhl_per_million)|round|int }} times the Czech NHL rate per inhabitant, and the Czech ranks stay the same under three different games thresholds.</li>
        <li>The Czech NHL count fell from {{ q1.peak.n }} players in {{ q1.peak.season }} to {{ q1.peak.latest.n }}; the break model spreads the timing of that fall over {{ q2.CZE.fall_spread[0] if q2.CZE.fall_spread else '–' }}–{{ q2.CZE.fall_spread[1] if q2.CZE.fall_spread else '–' }} and does not place it in one season.</li>
        <li>The Czech count is furthest below the peer median among players aged 21 or under, and skaters aged 20 or under take about half the share of league games at home that they take in the Liiga or the SHL.</li>
        <li>The counts are the whole published record rather than samples; averaged and modelled quantities carry intervals, and several groups are only a handful of players, so single-season ranks move easily.</li>
        <li>The atlas describes and does not explain: it identifies no cause, makes no forecast and gives no selection advice, and the KHL, which supplied about a quarter of Czech national-team roster spots, is outside its data.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>
    <dl class="meta-block mono">
      <div><dt>published</dt><dd>{{ meta.published }} · updated {{ meta.updated }} · <a href="#changes">version {{ meta.version }}</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>status</dt><dd>{{ meta.status }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>data</dt><dd>NHL, Liiga, SHL, Extraliga (hokej.cz), DEL, National League (SIHF), Eurostat <code>demo_gind</code> and English Wikipedia rosters; snapshot {{ meta.snapshot_date }}, hashes in <code>data/snapshot/SHA256SUMS</code> (sha256 {{ meta.snapshot_sums }}); <a href="methodology/#data-sources">data availability</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>code</dt><dd><a href="{{ meta.repo }}">{{ meta.repo_short }}</a>, <code>src/analysis/</code> and <code>src/web/</code>; rebuild: <code>{{ meta.rebuild }}</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt>cite as</dt><dd>Šandová, B. (2026). <em>{{ meta.title }}</em>. hockey.bsandova.com, version {{ meta.version }}.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>licence</dt><dd>code MIT; text and figures CC BY 4.0; roster-derived data CC BY-SA 4.0</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="front-question" id="question">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>The question and its contribution</h2>
    <p>Research on athlete development asks how players reach the top of a sport and which of them do. Relative age shapes who is selected in youth sport generally and in hockey in particular {{ ref(['cobley2009', 'nolan2010']) }}, success in youth national squads is followed by adult success for only some athletes {{ ref(['barreiros2014']) }}, world-class athletes tend to have practised several sports before specialising {{ ref(['gullich2022']) }}, and professional hockey moves players across national borders {{ ref(['maguire1996']) }}. Comparative work on national sport systems proposes a framework of policy factors behind international success {{ ref(['debosscher2006']) }}. This atlas tests none of these accounts. Its contribution is a descriptive base for the Czech case: from public league statistics and one definition of nationality, it counts how many Czech players reached the NHL and the four strongest European leagues relative to population, against nine peer nations over {{ q2.CZE.n_seasons }} seasons, and it publishes the counts, their intervals, the player list and the code that rebuilds them.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="take" id="take">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="close-kicker">Findings</h2>
    {% for t in take %}
    {% set q = questions[loop.index0] %}
    <div class="nx-take"><p class="nx-take-n">{{ loop.index }}</p><div><p class="nx-take-head">{{ t.head }}</p>{% for b in t.body %}<p class="nx-take-body">{{ b }}</p>{% endfor %}<p class="nx-take-link"><a href="{{ q.url }}">Question {{ q.n }}: {{ q.label }}</a></p></div></div>
    {% endfor %}
    <p class="take-line close-links"><a href="methodology/#scope">What is counted</a> · <a href="methodology/#limitations">Limitations</a> · <a href="players/">Every Czech player in the pool</a>{% if autumn %} · Note: <a href="this-autumn/">Czech hockey news, {{ autumn.news_as_of }}</a>{% endif %}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="front-foot" id="cite">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>How to cite</h2>
    <p>Šandová, B. (2026). <em>{{ meta.title }}</em>. hockey.bsandova.com, version {{ meta.version }}. <a href="{{ meta.url }}">{{ meta.url }}</a>. Code and data: <a href="{{ meta.repo }}">{{ meta.repo_short }}</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="references">References</h2>
    <ol class="references">
      {% for r in refs %}
      <li id="ref-{{ r.n }}">{{ r.text }} <a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.url }}</a>. Accessed {{ r.accessed }}.</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p>Data sources, with their access dates and terms, are listed under <a href="methodology/#data-sources">Data availability</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Change log</h2>
    <ul class="changelog">
      <li><span class="mono">29 September 2026</span> Version {{ meta.version }}: editorial pass to the site's editorial standard, with intervals added, a roster-linking correction and the corrected numbers listed in the <a href="methodology/#changes">full change log</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
